        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
        ":question/problem": "Calculate the integral $\\int \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{x\\ln{\\left(x^{4} \\right)}}\\,\\text{d}x.$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let's set $u=\\ln{\\left(x^{4} \\right)}.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x^{4}}\\cdot 4 x^{3}=\\frac{4}{x}\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{x\\ln{\\left(x^{4} \\right)}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\sqrt{3}\\int \\frac{1}{\\ln{\\left(x^{4} \\right)}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}\\ln|u|+C \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}\\ln|\\ln{\\left(x^{4} \\right)}|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
